The Monolith
************
A monolith runs everything in one process... 
Your user logic, order logic, payment logic are deployed together, sharing one database, one codebase...

Client  ──▶    MONOLITH [Users · Orders · Products · Payments · Email]  ──▶ One DB


Advantages of a monolith: 
************************
           - simple to run locally 
           - easy to debug (one log, one stack trace)
           - transactions are trivial (same DB)
           - low latency (in-process calls)
           - easy to refactor across modules.

Pain points at scale: 
********************
           - one team's deployment breaks everyone else's
           - you can't scale just the payments module
           - you scale everything, a bug in the email module can crash orders
           - the codebase becomes unmanageable after 50+ engineers.